+// This function queues an input packet the caller has built: an NV_INPUT_HEADER (the big-endian
+// size of the bytes after the size field, then the little-endian magic) and its payload, length
+// bytes in all (8 to 128). It goes on channelId, reliably or not. It's for protocol extensions
+// this library doesn't know, like LuzLunar's trackpad frames for anyosag/Apollo, so check the
+// host's LiGetHostFeatureFlags() first. Returns 0 when queued, -2 when not connected, -3 for a
+// malformed packet. (LuzLunar's patch, not upstream.)
+int LiSendForkInputPacket(const void* packet, uint32_t length, uint8_t channelId, bool reliable);
